            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 26,
              "start": 26
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kagan asked whether the petitioner was advocating a categorical rule that such marks would never be registrable."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f4c3f3173af07f0af8360a2540de16356c36266b5798e57bc795040ac55b18b9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f4c3f3173af0-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts questioned why the primary significance test, which is used for cancellation, should carry weight in a registration case."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f4c3f3173af07f0af8360a2540de16356c36266b5798e57bc795040ac55b18b9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f4c3f3173af0-0002-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 49,
              "start": 49
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justice Ginsburg noted that consumers associate the \u201c.com\u201d suffix with a particular source rather than a generic commodity."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f4c3f3173af07f0af8360a2540de16356c36266b5798e57bc795040ac55b18b9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f4c3f3173af0-0002-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 56,
              "start": 56
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked what the respondent\u2019s position would be if companies made slight variations of the Booking.com name and sought trademark protection."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f4c3f3173af07f0af8360a2540de16356c36266b5798e57bc795040ac55b18b9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f4c3f3173af0-0002-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 59,
              "start": 59
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked whether trademark applicants now must conduct consumer\u2011perception surveys before declaring a name generic."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f4c3f3173af07f0af8360a2540de16356c36266b5798e57bc795040ac55b18b9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f4c3f3173af0-0002-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 61,
              "start": 61
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor warned that if district courts are not given deference to the PTO, every court could end up re\u2011weighing the PTO\u2019s evidence on genericness."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f4c3f3173af07f0af8360a2540de16356c36266b5798e57bc795040ac55b18b9",
